       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose is above safe limits and may be a transcription error.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is **6400 mg/day**. That's twice the usual prescription maximum of 3200 mg/day for adults. Doses this high increase the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and heart problems, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n1. **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is common if \"1600\" was meant as the daily total.\n2. **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3200 mg/day). This is the maximum prescription dose.\n3. **600 mg by mouth four times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n\nPlease confirm which dose you meant, or give me a different one, and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll check with you again before entering an order that far above the limits."
      }
